\title{Formal Specification and Verification}
\date{2025-09-01}
\author{dhsorens}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    Formal verification is the practice of mathematically proving code to be \em{correct} with regards to a specification (a formal description).
    This can be done in many ways, most interestingly (in my opinion) within [interactive theorem provers](dhsorens-000B) like [Lean](dhsorens-lean) or [Rocq](dhsorens-rocq).
}
